    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d631">

                <pb facs="0608" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg524"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/3100</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-14T14:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 14, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.06 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7965. Your 5963, December 5, 8 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d631-f1"/> Government
                    here asks information about the present position of the United States in regard
                        <pb facs="0609" n="525" xml:id="pg525"/> to issue of licenses for
                    remittances to enemy and enemy-occupied territory and would like to know what
                    remittances have been authorized. They feel they should exercise vigilance but
                    do not wish to place any hindrance in the way of passage of remittances which
                    United States has licensed and may wish to go forward.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
